      "interpretation": "MULTIPATH CHARACTERISATION ONLY. 96.7% (median) of the double-difference residual variance is sidereal-repeating, i.e. multipath: leave-one-day-out sidereal cleaning drops the DD residual from 79-145 mm to 13-31 mm. That part stands. The post-cleaning holonomy slopes (|z| <= 1.6) are NOT a bound on the non-exact sector and must not be reported as one: the loop invariant T is a function of satellite geometry, and satellite geometry is exactly what repeats every sidereal day, so the template removes a static geometry-locked signal along with the multipath. step_72 shows by injection that a static holonomy is recovered at 1.00 of its true slope before cleaning and 0.00 after, on all eight pairs, while a day-modulated injection survives at 1.26. The non-exact sector is therefore UNTESTED on this dataset, not bounded. Separating it requires a site-frame azimuth/elevation multipath model (multipath is a per-satellite, per-site function of az/el; T is an irreducibly two-satellite cross-product), not day-repetition.",
